---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Services"
  description="Website and digital presence development, business systems and process automation, and custom digital solutions for SMEs and growing organisations."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="container page-head__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Services</p>
        <h1 class="h1">Systems that fit<br />the way you work.</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="lede">
        We work across three connected areas. A project may sit in one of them, or
        move from a public website into the operational system behind it. We scope
        each engagement around your requirements rather than selling a fixed
        package.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="sticky-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">A / Digital presence</p>
          <h2 class="h2">Website and digital presence development</h2>
          <p class="lede mt-1">
            A website should do more than look current. It should explain the
            offer clearly, earn trust, and make the next step obvious on a phone
            as well as a desktop.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="callout">
            <p>
              <strong>Problems this solves:</strong> an outdated site that
              undersells the business, unclear service pages, enquiries arriving
              in scattered messages, a catalogue that is hard to update, or a
              booking process that depends on back and forth phone calls.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="grid grid--2 mt-2">
            <div class="card">
              <h3>Typical deliverables</h3>
              <ul class="card__list">
                <li>Business and corporate websites</li>
                <li>E-commerce stores and product catalogues</li>
                <li>Landing pages for campaigns and launches</li>
                <li>Booking and enquiry websites</li>
                <li>Redesigns with clearer structure and copy</li>
                <li>Content management for routine updates</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <h3>What good looks like</h3>
              <ul class="card__list">
                <li>Readable on a small phone screen</li>
                <li>Fast loading on ordinary mobile data</li>
                <li>Clear calls to action and enquiry routes</li>
                <li>Search and social previews that make sense</li>
                <li>An editing workflow your team can follow</li>
                <li>Analytics and forms connected correctly</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="callout mt-2">
            <p>
              <strong>Good fit if</strong> you need a credible public presence, a
              catalogue people can browse, or a simpler way for customers to
              enquire or book. A website can also be the first phase before an
              internal system is added.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="sticky-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">B / Operations</p>
          <h2 class="h2">Business systems and process automation</h2>
          <p class="lede mt-1">
            Most growing businesses reach a point where spreadsheets, WhatsApp
            threads and memory stop being enough. We map the process, remove the
            avoidable steps, and build a system the team can rely on.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="callout">
            <p>
              <strong>Problems this solves:</strong> stock records that disagree,
              orders tracked in several places, leads that are never followed up,
              bookings managed by hand, reports that take hours to assemble, or
              one person holding all the operational knowledge.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="grid grid--2 mt-2">
            <div class="card">
              <h3>Typical deliverables</h3>
              <ul class="card__list">
                <li>CRM and customer records</li>
                <li>Lead, enquiry and follow up tracking</li>
                <li>Inventory, products and stock control</li>
                <li>Orders, bookings and scheduling</li>
                <li>Task assignment and workflow automation</li>
                <li>Reporting dashboards and exports</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <h3>What good looks like</h3>
              <ul class="card__list">
                <li>One source of truth for the team</li>
                <li>Clear roles and permissions</li>
                <li>Statuses that match how work actually moves</li>
                <li>Useful notifications, not noise</li>
                <li>Reports that answer real questions</li>
                <li>Written process notes and training</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="callout mt-2">
            <p>
              <strong>Good fit if</strong> the business has outgrown manual
              tracking, or if several tools exist but do not talk to each other.
              We can improve an existing setup, replace it, or connect the pieces
              that are worth keeping.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="sticky-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">C / Custom build</p>
          <h2 class="h2">Custom digital solutions</h2>
          <p class="lede mt-1">
            Some processes are specific enough that no standard product fits. In
            those cases we design and build a focused application around the way
            your organisation actually works.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="callout">
            <p>
              <strong>Problems this solves:</strong> a programme managed across
              documents and spreadsheets, partners or members needing a portal, a
              field team working from paper, or an internal process that cannot be
              bought off the shelf without changing the business to suit it.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="grid grid--2 mt-2">
            <div class="card">
              <h3>Typical deliverables</h3>
              <ul class="card__list">
                <li>Web applications and customer portals</li>
                <li>Membership and programme platforms</li>
                <li>Android, iPhone and cross platform apps</li>
                <li>Internal tools and operational dashboards</li>
                <li>Role based access and approval flows</li>
                <li>Integrations with payment, email and calendar tools</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <h3>What good looks like</h3>
              <ul class="card__list">
                <li>The scope starts small and solves a real problem</li>
                <li>The data model matches the business rules</li>
                <li>Every role sees only what it needs</li>
                <li>Important actions are logged and reversible where possible</li>
                <li>The system can be maintained after handover</li>
                <li>Costs and limitations are stated plainly</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="callout mt-2">
            <p>
              <strong>Good fit if</strong> your process is a genuine source of
              advantage, or if the available products force costly workarounds.
              We will say when a simpler tool would serve you better.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--ink">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Scoping</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Not every project needs a custom application.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="lede">
          We start with the smallest solution that can solve the problem well. That
          might be a well structured website, a configured existing tool, a
          focused integration, or a custom build. The recommendation follows the
          requirement, not the other way round.
        </p>
        <ul class="check-list mt-2">
          <li>Discovery and process mapping before a build commitment</li>
          <li>A written scope with assumptions, exclusions and acceptance criteria</li>
          <li>Phased delivery where the first release can go live early</li>
          <li>Clear ownership of accounts, domains and source files</li>
          <li>Handover, documentation and training included in the plan</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Start with the problem, not the software."
    text="Describe the process that is causing friction. We will help you decide whether it needs a website, a system, a smaller fix, or nothing at all."
    primaryLabel="Discuss a project"
    secondaryLabel="See how we work"
    secondaryHref="/how-we-work"
  />
</BaseLayout>
